Third-party notices
===================

This project includes code ported from the following open-source software.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LibreChat
https://github.com/danny-avila/LibreChat
License: MIT

Ported (translated to TypeScript and adapted to this project's data model):
- packages/importers: the ChatGPT, Claude and LibreChat export importers and
  the conversation fork modes, from api/server/utils/import/importers.js,
  api/server/utils/import/fork.js, packages/api/src/conversations/chatgpt.ts
  and packages/api/src/conversations/lineage.ts (reference revision
  7b2362d7a7c6148b84850924dc7fa5fc43307923).
- packages/mcp: LibreChat's MCP connection management (packages/api/src/mcp:
  MCPManager, UserConnectionManager, ConnectionsRepository, MCPConnection, the
  MCP OAuth handler and token storage, MCPServersRegistry, and
  normalizeServerName from packages/data-provider), as of commit 7b2362d
  (2026-09-25). The logic was rewritten as functions over the AI SDK's
  @ai-sdk/mcp client: shared vs per-user connections, reconnect backoff with
  jitter, the connection circuit breaker and its defaults, the 429 stop,
  tool-list limits, idle eviction, the per-user OAuth flow with state binding
  and client-registration reuse, and server-name normalisation for tool names.

